    "body": "Closes #8006 (albeit in an unsatisfactory way).\r\n\r\nThese features are incompatible because they use global cdef variables (which are currently outside the module state). I've already added existing warnings for that feature in user code but the `subinterpreters_compatible` flag doesn't make it into the utility code.\r\n\r\nI think the easiest fix is to add a special-cased warning for these two bits of utility code. I've tried to do it in a semi-generic way rather than just checking a hardcoded list of names. I don't think any other Cython utility code should have this problem (although there's undoubtedly bits of global state that I haven't spotted elsewhere).",
    "closed_at": null,
