                    "name": "da-woods"
                },
                "message": "Add warnings for subinterpreters for memoryviews and enums\n\nCloses #8006 (albeit in an unsatisfactory way).\n\nThese features are incompatible because they use global cdef\nvariables (which are currently outside the module state). I've\nalready added existing warnings for that feature in user code\nbut the `subinterpreters_compatible` flag doesn't make it into\nthe utility code.\n\nI think the easiest fix is to add a special-cased warning for\nthese two bits of utility code. I've tried to do it in a\nsemi-generic way rather than just checking a hardcoded list of\nnames. I don't think any other Cython utility code should have this\nproblem (although there's undoubtedly bits of global state\nthat I haven't spotted elsewhere).",
